(7519793, 1201223, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>I like the abstract nature of this water in motion, you have a nice diagonal that gives the image a more dynamic feel. I also like the tones you have ranging from the near white of the crest to the darker right though I wish there was a little more of that to balance it up a bit more. All in all really quite appealing, thanks Janine.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge well I like the abstract nature of this water in motion, you have a nice diagonal that gives the image a more dynamic feel. I also like the tones you have ranging from the near white of the crest to the darker right though I wish there was a little more of that to balance it up a bit more. All in all really quite appealing, thanks Janine.', '2017-06-22 08:57:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7519805, 1201253, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>Congratulations Konrad on your blue and winning this challenge. The motion blur in the water is most appealing together with your considered composition including the foreground rock around which the waters are spilling was a sensible decision. I do have one criticism in that the seas horizon appears to be leaning to the right a little. The clouds in the sky are a nice addition to the overall result, all in all most pleasing.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge well Congratulations Konrad on your blue and winning this challenge. The motion blur in the water is most appealing together with your considered composition including the foreground rock around which the waters are spilling was a sensible decision. I do have one criticism in that the seas horizon appears to be leaning to the right a little. The clouds in the sky are a nice addition to the overall result, all in all most pleasing.', '2017-06-22 10:19:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7519807, 1201267, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An interesting image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>A pleasing composition Marcel, the shape of the water in motion is appealing together with its reflections. The person gives a sense of scale and is nicely positioned but the lamppost is not so good but there is little within the rules that you could do about that. What lets it all down for me is the serious banding in the sky which is most surprising given the minimal editing rules, it really is immediately obvious to a detrimental level. I quite like the building its position and lighting it does add to the image.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An interesting image that meets the challenge well A pleasing composition Marcel, the shape of the water in motion is appealing together with its reflections. The person gives a sense of scale and is nicely positioned but the lamppost is not so good but there is little within the rules that you could do about that. What lets it all down for me is the serious banding in the sky which is most surprising given the minimal editing rules, it really is immediately obvious to a detrimental level. I quite like the building its position and lighting it does add to the image.', '2017-06-22 10:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7519856, 1201253, 112739, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the Blue. Beautiful seascape!</td>', 'Congratulations on the Blue. Beautiful seascape!', '2017-06-22 16:07:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7520457, 1201190, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congrats Lynn. I love this.</td>', 'Congrats Lynn. I love this.', '2017-06-26 23:22:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7525273, 1201114, 136989, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/>I lived in Arizona for a few years where we often looked for scorpions with black lights.  The blue of the UV light here is much prettier (than the yellow-green we had) and I agree that the scorpion is quite "striking". I''m really impressed with the clarity given the one second exposure requirement. <br/> <br/>I''m torn about the composition.  I love the upper third but feel like the lower third is mostly negative (uninteresting) space.  I would struggle to crop off the centipede''s body too, so that is where I am torn. The exposure is great.  You can see the legs of the prey against the background with nice detail. The branch and leaves are also well light without illuminating the darkness behind that creates such a beautiful contrast with the UV blue of the scorpion.<br/> <br/>Congrats on a top 10 finish!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!I lived in Arizona for a few years where we often looked for scorpions with black lights.  The blue of the UV light here is much prettier (than the yellow-green we had) and I agree that the scorpion is quite "striking". I''m really impressed with the clarity given the one second exposure requirement.  I''m torn about the composition.  I love the upper third but feel like the lower third is mostly negative (uninteresting) space.  I would struggle to crop off the centipede''s body too, so that is where I am torn. The exposure is great.  You can see the legs of the prey against the background with nice detail. The branch and leaves are also well light without illuminating the darkness behind that creates such a beautiful contrast with the UV blue of the scorpion. Congrats on a top 10 finish!', '2017-07-24 17:35:00.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
